    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0157" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1380: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-10T11:00:00-06:00">January 10,
                            1939—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. Referring to telegram No. 98, January 6, 11 a.m., from Ocheltree at San Jose.
                    Discreet inquiry reveals reasons the Honduran Government took the position
                    mentioned was apparently because the same proposal as to survey was made in
                        1930<anchor n="14" xml:id="d199-f1"/> under another administration. <pb
                        facs="0158" n="150" xml:id="pg150"/> After mature consideration decision was
                    reached that approval now would be subject to political misrepresentation in
                    Honduras and apparent change of policy could be used to inflame population.
                    Division among President’s advisers with group represented by Silverio Lainez,
                    Julian Lopez Pineda, and Romulo Duron, supported by the Foreign Minister,
                    convincing the President against acceptance of the proposal.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Dr. Corrigan at Panama City.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Erwin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
